Lekhoni — Bangla phonetic IME for Windows
=========================================

Scope of this license
---------------------

The MIT License below applies to:

  * all source code under src/, tools/, and tests/;
  * build, package, and installation scripts;
  * documentation;
  * data/source/starter.tsv, data/source/phrases.tsv, and data/source/eval.tsv,
    which are original work authored for this project.

Data files keep their upstream licenses
---------------------------------------

The remaining files under data/ derive from third-party sources. They are NOT
covered by the MIT grant and are licensed under — and redistributable only
under the terms of — their upstream licenses. The provenance of each file is
recorded in data/README.md:

  data/compiled/LekhoniCore.merged.bgk       GPL-2.0-or-later  (Avro Keyboard Database.db3)
  data/source/imported-core.tsv              GPL-2.0-or-later, with MPL-2.0 portions (Lekho suffix forms)
  data/source/imported-keys.tsv              GPL-2.0-or-later  (derived from the merged corpus)
  data/source/imported-autodict.tsv          MPL-2.0 (Lekho) with GPL-derived merges (Avro autodict)
  data/source/imported-autodict-caps.tsv     same lineage as imported-autodict.tsv
  data/compiled/avro-layout.dat              GPL-2.0-or-later  (OpenBangla avrophonetic.json)
  data/compiled/LekhoniTrigrams.dat          CC BY-SA 3.0 / GFDL (Bengali Wikipedia)
  data/source/corpus/                        CC BY-SA 3.0 / GFDL (Bengali Wikipedia)

Compiled dictionaries under artifacts/ are build outputs and inherit the
status of their inputs. The full texts of the upstream licenses are kept in
third-party-licenses/, and the per-project attribution and derivation record
is in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Release packages that contain third-party-
derived data ship both, together with the source-form TSVs, so the archive
can be redistributed as-is under those terms.

For a package covered by the MIT License alone, build with
`build.ps1 -UseStarterDictionary` (or `package.ps1 -UseStarterDictionary`).

If you obtained a copy of any data file from a third party rather than from
this repository, that third party's terms apply to it.


